                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_426">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Balliol College (Domus de Balliolo). </orgName><p>Many late-13th- and
                        14th-cent. notes of pledging. ‘While thus pledged, the volume was bequeathed
                        to Balliol. at the head of 1, over another note now erased, is: Iste liber
                        legatus erat domui de Balliolo in Oxonia per Magistrum Edmundum de Mepeham
                        qui quidem liber inveniebatur expositus in cista de Vahghan pro v s. et vj
                        d. quam pecuniam solvit domus predicta dicte ciste librum extrahendo die
                        sancte Lucie virginis A.D. moccco tricesimo. on 2 is: Egidius super librum
                        Elencorum de anima super librum posteriorum per Mepham. There is another
                        list of contents on 3v [. . .] and the late 14th-cent. College
                        inventory-mark 99 expositor logice is on 4.’ (Mynors, Balliol,
                     99)</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Edmund Mepham (d. 1333), canon of Llandaff
